# =============================================================================
# MikeOS daemon-as-system — SELinux file_contexts (first draft).
#
# Labels the daemon's launcher (so init can transition into the mikedaemon
# domain) and the daemon's data tree (so the domain may manage it).
#
# KNOWN-UNVERIFIED (see ../README.md):
#   * The launcher path. We install it to /system/bin/mikeos-daemon (per the
#     spec). If a build constraint moves it to /vendor/bin, update this regex to
#     /vendor/bin/mikeos-daemon and keep the type an *_exec vendor_file_type.
#   * /data/mikeos labeling — regex must win over the generic /data(/.*)? rule;
#     more-specific paths take precedence in file_contexts, so this is fine, but
#     verify with `ls -Z /data/mikeos` on the first boot.
# =============================================================================

# The init-launched hardened launcher -> exec type (drives the domain transition).
/system/bin/mikeos-daemon    u:object_r:mikedaemon_exec:s0

# The daemon's absolute data root and everything under it.
/data/mikeos(/.*)?           u:object_r:mikeos_data_file:s0
